        "note": "Still failing after 3 attempts. Last diagnosis: The timeout error detection in src/status.js line 9 checks `err.code === 'ABORT_ERR'`, but node-fetch 3.3.2 does not use a `code` property for timeout errors. Instead, timeout errors are AbortError instances with `err.name === 'AbortError'` and `err.cause.name === 'AbortError'` (or similar cause chain). The check for `err.code === 'ABORT_ERR'` will never match, causing timeout errors to fall through to the 'down' classification. This is why test/status.test.js:21 fails with \"Missing expected rejection\" (the timeout error is not being thrown as expected) and test/status.test.js:34 expects 'timeout' but gets 'ok' (the timeout is not being detected, so the request appears to succeed)."
